  {
    "episode_id": 85887,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/5/85887.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, it's awful. And it's something I never thought I would experience, not just the attack on the Capitol and the fear of violence, effort to stop the transfer of power for the first time in history. but also to see the Justice Department where I served for almost six years become a kind of a criminal defense firm for the president or worse. We used to go after the president's enemies to wonder as others did, are they going to turn that apparatus against me? That's the kind of experience you have in the third world, not in what should be the most secure democracy in the world. Those were showing things and you're absolutely right. The guardrails came close to failing and a number of those are under continuing assault. One of the guardrails that held was the House itself. Kevin McCarthy tried to overturn the election in the House. A vast majority of Republicans voted to overturn the presidential election. And if they were to gain control of the House in the midterms, Ken McCarthy would overturn the presidential election in 2024 if Donald Trump loses. And so that's a guardrail that's very much at risk. and underscores, I think, the importance of making sure that someone of the kind of low character and morals of Kevin McCarthy never goes near the speaker's office anymore than Donald Trump goes near the office. But you know, one other guardrail that held was that local and state elections officials, Democrats and Republicans did their jobs. And one of the takeaways of Trump and his enablers seems to be that if they couldn't get the Secretary of State in Georgia, for example, to find 11,780 votes that don't exist, they're determined to have someone in that job and others around the country who next time will. And even local technocratic elections personnel are being run out of their post with death threats. So these are the guardrails that are currently under assault. We need to pay attention to. We need to shore up.",
