  {
    "episode_id": 85887,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/5/85887.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Especially the laws now that are passing in the wake of the big line, not just voter suppression laws, though they fall under that umbrella, but the laws where in certain states they want the state legislature, because like you, we were talking about what if nobody gets to 270? Oh, well, then it goes to the house, et cetera, et cetera. And we were thinking of that there were states who wanted to send alternate slates of electors, and we're actively talking about that. And we sort of laughed it off like you can't just overturn the will of the voters and send your own electors. And besides, the laws don't allow that for that right now, as we've seen from memos to Wisconsin and Arizona back in 2020. You know, we were like, how go ahead and try to pass that law, I dare you. Go ahead and try to pass a law that says, no matter how you vote, we, the state legislature, are going to determine who the electors are, yet they're doing it.",
