    "turn_text": "That's exactly right. And to me, that is the most chilling of all. These efforts to disenfranchise people are just pernicious in a return to the kind of bigotry of Jim Crow many years ago, a new generation of Jim Crow. But the efforts at election subversion to empower Republican boards and legislatures to essentially overturn the popular will if they don't like what voters do. That is a terrifying attack on the infrastructure of our democracy. They're really taking a page out of Victor Orban, the wannabe dictator and Hungary's playbook, using the instruments of democracy against itself. Not relying the next time on a violent insurrection, but relying on positive legal beings. to diminish our democracy to the point where they can undermine the results of a presidential election. And to me that is among the most fragile points of our democracy at present.",
