  {
    "episode_id": 85887,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/5/85887.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "One other point I would add to that, which was really a main takeaway for me coming out of the first impeachment or the second impeachment. And that is having a brilliant constitution is not enough. Having well framed laws is not enough. Having pernicious laws like they're trying to pass this even worse, of course. But at the end of the day, we are reliant on members of the legislature and if Congress honoring their oath of office. Being informed by it is right and wrong, and having some devotion to the truth. And if none of those factors are present, if members will just ignore the truth, propagate a big line or a bunch of small ones, or believe that to anything they do that helps perpetuate themselves in power makes it right, none of it works. And so we're facing, I think, a crisis in which one of America's two great parties has been up being a party of ideas, has given up being a party devoted to democracy, has become a kind of autocratic cult of the former president, and that puts us on a very perilous fight.",
